<title>DUBAI: World's largest oil tanker arriving in Dubai.</title>
<headline>World's largest oil tanker arriving in Dubai.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The world's largest oil tanker is scheduled to arrive at Dubai Dry Docks on Tuesday to undergo three weeks of general repairs, a Gulf shipping source said.</p>
<p>The Norwegian-flagged 564,763 dwt ultra large crude carrier (ULCC) Jahre Viking is used regularly to transport crude oil from Saudi Arabia to the U.S. Gulf coast.</p>
<p>&quot;The vessel is arriving today,&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>Dubai is one of the seven members that make up the Gulf state of the United Arab Emirates.</p>
<p>-- Steven Swindells, Dubai Newsroom, +971 4 6071255.</p>
</text>
